<p>Without any exemptions, the same home would owe about $8,501. The exemptions in this example save roughly $1,950 a year, and the effective rate drops to about 1.64% of market value. If other units also grant exemptions on your account, your bill would be lower still; if you are in a MUD, add that district's tax.</p>
